quickAnswer:'Makara Sankranti 2026 falls on Wednesday, 14 January. It is a solar festival marking the Sun’s entry into Makara, or Capricorn, and is celebrated through harvest, Surya worship, food, family and regional traditions such as Pongal in Tamil Nadu.',
keyTakeaways:['Makara Sankranti 2026 is on 14 January.','It is based on a solar transition rather than a lunar tithi.','Pongal is a major Tamil harvest festival in the same seasonal period.','Regional practices include kite flying, sesame sweets, cattle worship and river bathing.','The common thread is gratitude for food, land, Sun and seasonal renewal.'],
