quickAnswer:'Hanuman Jayanti 2026 falls on Thursday, 2 April in the widely followed Chaitra Purnima tradition. Regional traditions can observe Hanuman’s birth on different dates, so the festival is not uniform across India.',
keyTakeaways:['A widely followed Hanuman Jayanti date in 2026 is 2 April.','Regional traditions use different dates.','Hanuman is associated with Anjana and Vayu in birth traditions.','His strength is repeatedly placed in service of Rama.','Hanuman worship often includes Hanuman Chalisa, Sundara Kanda and Rama nama.'],
faq:[
{question:'When is Hanuman Jayanti in 2026?',answer:'A widely followed North Indian Hanuman Jayanti falls on Thursday, 2 April 2026, on Chaitra Purnima. Some regional traditions observe Hanuman’s birth on other dates.'},
{question:'Who are Hanuman’s parents?',answer:'Hanuman is commonly remembered as the son of Anjana and Kesari, with Vayu playing a divine role in his birth and therefore giving rise to names such as Vayuputra.'},
{question:'Why is Hanuman so closely linked to Rama?',answer:'The Ramayana makes Hanuman one of Rama’s greatest servants and devotees. His power is repeatedly used for Rama, Sita and dharma rather than personal status.'},
{question:'What is recited on Hanuman Jayanti?',answer:'Common recitations include Hanuman Chalisa, Sundara Kanda, Hanuman stotras and Rama nama, depending on region and family tradition.'}
],
body:[
{paragraphs:['Hanuman Jayanti is observed on 2 April in 2026 in the widely followed Chaitra Purnima tradition. But Hanuman’s birth is celebrated on different dates in different parts of India, so one date should not be presented as universal.','That variation suits Hanuman in a strange way. He belongs everywhere: temples, village shrines, wrestling akharas, Ramayana recitations, roadside sanctums and personal prayer.']},
{heading:'What is Hanuman’s birth story?',paragraphs:['Hanuman is commonly remembered as the son of Anjana and Kesari, with Vayu, the wind deity, playing a divine role in his birth. This is why names such as Vayuputra and Maruti are used for him.','Different texts and regions tell the birth story with variations. The shared memory is of extraordinary power arriving in a being who will later choose service over self-display.']},
{heading:'Why is Hanuman’s strength different?',paragraphs:['Hanuman can leap across the ocean, carry a mountain and terrify armies. Yet the centre of his character is not power alone. It is power offered to Rama.','That changes the meaning of strength. The question is not “How strong am I?” but “What does my strength serve?”']},
{heading:'Why is Sundara Kanda important?',paragraphs:['Sundara Kanda tells Hanuman’s journey to Lanka, his discovery of Sita and his return with hope. It is one of the most beloved sections of the Ramayana for recitation.','The episode combines courage, intelligence, restraint and devotion. Hanuman must know when to become vast and when to become small.']},
{heading:'How can the day be observed?',paragraphs:['Recite Hanuman Chalisa or Sundara Kanda if that belongs to your practice. Chant Rama’s name. Visit a Hanuman temple. Offer food or service.','The most Hanuman-like act may be useful work done without demanding applause.']}
],
sources:[{label:'Valmiki Ramayana, especially Sundara Kanda',note:'Primary epic context for Hanuman’s service to Rama and Sita.'},{label:'Regional Hanuman birth traditions',note:'Used to explain why Hanuman Jayanti dates differ across India.'}],
